credentials are offered at the graduate level: certificate, diploma, master\u2019s, and doctoral.\nResearch + Innovation at SFU\nSFU is home to a variety of world-class research facilities and world-renowned scholars.\nLearn why you should join us\nCredential Requirements\nTo be granted a credential, a student must satisfy requirements at two level to ensure a depth of study:\nUniversity-wide requirements\nProgram requirements as set by the department, school or program defining the area of study\nIn master\u2019s or doctoral programs students may be given additional requirements by their supervisor or graduate program committee.\nTransfer Credential Subject\nA student may be admitted to one credential and transfer to a different credential subject to meeting requirements. If a student transfers to a more advanced credential they will only receive the highest credential upon fulfilling the requirements.\nPrograms\nWe offer a wide variety of program options for you to build your own graduate student experience. Master's and doctoral degrees are available in all eight of our faculties.\nLearn more about our programs\nApplying for Admission\nTake the time to review our deadlines and requirements to ensure your admission process goes smoothly. Applying is easy with our 4-step application process.\nLearn more about applying\nTuition and Fees\nAll graduate students are charged tuition each term of their enrollment. Find out the cost of tuition and fees for the program you want to enroll in.\nLearn more about tuition and fees\nVisiting and Incoming Exchange\nFor current graduate students at other institutions interested in conducting research or taking courses at SFU. We also offer non-degree options.\nLearn more about our non-degree options\nFaculty of Graduate Studies\nAbout\nApply\nAwards + Funding\nGraduate Students\nLife + Community\nContact us\nFaculty of Graduate Studies\nMaggie Benston Centre 1100\nSimon Fraser University\n8888 University Drive\nBurnaby, B.C.\nCana